Regular expressions: 
	A regular expression is a smart rule that checks wheather text follows a specific pattern.
	Regex regular expression in java is a pattern used to match,search,validate,split or replace text.
	java provides regex support through the java.util.regex package
	
Regular Expressions are used:
	To validate input(email, mobile number, password)
	To search text efficiently
	To extract specific data from strings
	To replace or split strings based on patterns
	
Main classes:
	Pattern - represents the regex pattern
	Matcher - matches the pattern against a string
Pattern defines the rule,and matcher applies that rule to the data

Regex is a powerful way to define patterns for matching and validating Strings in java
Basic regex syntax starts with matching excat text, understnading case sensitivity, and performing simple pattern checks

Regex symbols are used to define rules for matching text patterns

Some important patterns:

. = Matches any single character except newline.
+ = Matches one or more occurences of the previous character or pattern
* = Matches zero or more occurences of the previous character or pattern
? = zero or one occurence  of the preceding character / group
\d = Matches any single digit from 0 to 9
\w = Matches letters, digits and underscore only  - no spaces or special characters.
\s = Matches any whitespace character such as space, tab or newline
[A-Z] = Matches any one uppercase letter from A to Z
[a -z] = Matches any one lowercase letter from a to z
abc = Matches excat sequence of  characters abc ina string
{n} = Matches exact sequence of the preceeding character or group
{n,m} = is used when the number of repetitions must fall within a specific range
| OR = allows matching one pattern OR another, and growing with () is highly recommended.

